      "origin": {
        "handoffEntry": "MIK-R39@v1-focus-request-answered-by-its-selection",
        "leaf": "260928-MIK-L39"
      },
      "rationale": "Its `refreshReview` leaves a request that only scrolls and remembers the read on screen at the click. Its `settle` drops that request when the read on screen is failed or refused and is not the one remembered, and remembers that read as the refresh's failure. Its `retryReview` settles first and then is the refresh again when the read on screen is that failure; otherwise it only reads again. The cases \"forgets the scroll a refresh asked for when its read fails, so a later page of the subject leaves the rail alone\", \"brings the selected row into view after a refresh asked in the turn that shows a failed read\" and \"brings the selected row into view when the retry is made in the turn that shows the failed refresh\" of `dashboard/src/panels/review/ReviewSurface.walkFresh.test.tsx` test these three paths.",
      "role": "primary-authority"
    },
    {
      "anchor": {
        "blob": "24598572b515687b4e415de48aa409de53d81d1f",
        "content": "sha256:2bea560c5f336151a88c4c7f72860d44ec8070841375b4f546fdeee71624801b",
        "locator": {
          "kind": "symbol",
          "name": "useRefreshReview"
        }
      },
      "id": "RLZ-FRKWFP",
      "invariant": "INV-9ZKYWQ",
      "origin": {
        "handoffEntry": "MIK-R39@v1-other-selections-start-afresh",
        "leaf": "260928-MIK-L39"
      },
      "rationale": "Its `refreshReview` begins a selection that does not keep before it asks the read cycle to read again, so a refresh shows the comparison as it reads now and not the tree walked before it. The case \"starts afresh at a refresh of the review\" of `dashboard/src/panels/review/ReviewSurface.walkFresh.test.tsx` tests it.",
      "role": "enforcement"
    },
    {
